Change history:

1.0.10 - craigde - Report requests the cloud rejects instead of dropping them.
         Every websocket#api reply carries its own HTTP-style status code, and
         a refused request still arrives as a perfectly ordinary message - so
         nothing threw, the send looked successful, and the failure was
         invisible. That is why a dishwasher pod-count command that the cloud
         refuses looked like nothing happening at all.
         interpretResponse() now checks that status first and logs a warning
         with the reason the cloud gave (e.g. "erd is not writable") before
         dispatching. Appliance control commands also get a correlation id now
         (smarthqHelpers buildAppCtrlSetter previously sent an empty id,
         matching the reference python SDK), so their replies are matched to
         the command that caused them rather than logged as an unrecognized
         message. Also: sendWssMap() no longer forwards a null message, which
         used to put the literal string "null" on the socket when a builder
         bailed out.
1.0.7  - Alan (patched) - Replaced the two resp.data.'**' GPath deep-search
         calls (in get_authorization_code()'s login-page fetch and in
         skipMfaPrompt()'s MFA-page fetch) with textParser:true + regex
         extraction via a new extractAttr() helper. On the latest Hubitat
         firmware, the internal HTTP client changed (now
         com.hubitat.hub.executor.helpers.ExecutorHttpClient5) and no longer
         reliably auto-parses these responses into a GPathResult, causing
         "No such property: **" MissingPropertyException and breaking login
         entirely on that firmware. Forcing textParser:true and pulling
         'signature' / '_csrf' out with a regex avoids depending on Hubitat's
         implicit HTML auto-parse behavior.
1.0.6  - craigde - Login flow hardening + MFA-prompt handling.
         (1) Harden the OAuth authorization-code parsing. The login redirect
         query-string parser used temp[1] after split("="), which threw
         ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException when GE returned an empty-valued redirect
         param (e.g. "scope="), breaking full re-auth. Parsing now splits on the
         first '=' only and tolerates valueless params (shared parseRedirectParams
         helper used by both redirect-parse sites).
         (2) Auto-skip GE's non-persistent "test MFA" interstitial. When the
         login redirect lands on the MFA prompt, the app now replicates the
         website's "Skip" action (fetch the MFA page for a fresh _csrf, then POST
         an empty mfaType to the redirect endpoint) and continues to the real
         code redirect. MFA-skip flow contributed by youzer-name (GitHub PR #12).
         (3) When login still returns no authorization code (MFA wall, bad
         credentials, or a changed flow) the app logs a clear reason and shows it
         on the config page instead of failing silently into the reconnect backoff.
1.0.0  - craigde - Refactored from device driver to app architecture

*/

